quran[26]{c,v,t}:
  37,77,We made his descendants the only survivors.
  37,78,And We left for him (an honourable mention) among later generations.
  37,79,‘Peace be upon Nuh (Noah) throughout the nations!’
  37,80,"Indeed, this is how We reward the virtuous."
  37,81,"Surely, he was among Our faithful servants."
  37,82,Then We drowned the others.
  37,83,"Indeed, one of those who followed his way was Ibrahim (Abraham)."
  37,84,"When he came to his Lord with a submissive, sound heart,"
  37,85,and said to his (foster) father and his people: ‘What are you worshipping?
  37,86,"Do you desire false gods, by perversion, besides Allah?"
  37,87,"So, what do you expect from the Lord of all worlds?’"
  37,88,Then he looked up to the stars as an observation.
  37,89,"And said: ‘Indeed, I am sick (of your worshipping these things).’"
  37,90,"So, they went away from him, turning (their) backs."
  37,91,Then he went quietly to their gods and said (mockingly): ‘Do you not eat (from your offerings)?
  37,92,Why do you not speak?’
  37,93,"Then, he turned upon them, striking (and breaking) them forcefully."
  37,94,"Later, they came running towards him."
  37,95,"He said: ‘Do you worship what you carve (with your hands),"
  37,96,while Allah has created you and whatever you do?’
  37,97,They said: ‘Build a structure and throw him into the blazing fire.’
  37,98,"They desired to scheme against him, but We made them the lowest (thus defeating them in their plan)."
  37,99,He said (while migrating to Syria): ‘I am going to my Lord. He will certainly guide me.’
  37,100,"‘My Lord, bless me with (a son) among the righteous.’"
  37,101,So We gave him the glad tidings of a gentle son. (And he was Isma‘il [Ishmael]).
  37,102,"When he (Isma‘il) reached the age to work alongside him, he (Ibrahim) said (to him): ‘My dear son! I have seen in a dream that I am sacrificing you. So think, what is your opinion?’ He (Isma‘il) replied: ‘My dear father! Do whatever you are commanded. If Allah pleases, you will find me among the patient.’"
